  "changes": [
    "Sibling navigation filenames adapted for /games/ hosting.",
    "Direct first-chapter entry redirects to the shared host for progress preservation.",
    "Local-file comment adapted for hosting.",
    "Three.js MIT notice retained.",
    "Embedded image/music literals line-wrapped with unchanged runtime bytes.",
    "v17: second chapter drops four unused embedded bitmaps (backdrop, kelpBackdrop, fish, turtle); map and first chapter unchanged from v16.",
    "v18: map adds a return-to-handbook link; second chapter welcome card keeps only chapter, title and start; sample label removed.",
    "v19: unchanged original images/music and classic runtime scripts served as hash-named static assets; map exposes explicit loading/retry state and sends host readiness only after both visible images have loaded.",
    "v20: first-chapter host selection occurs before second-chapter WebGL loading; mobile first-chapter run button removed; coarse-pointer rendering capped at 1.5 DPR with bounded fixed-step catch-up for smoother steering; two cockpit pilot images and their runtime references removed.",
    "v21: map shell and controls become interactive without waiting for decorative images; first chapter starts after five critical images while remaining art loads in the background; first chapter loading mark no longer mirrors fallback text; second chapter WebGL initializes only when selected; coarse-pointer rendering uses a 1.25 DPR cap, two-step catch-up, and one camera collision solve per rendered frame.",
    "v22: second chapter prepares shaders, shadows, the cockpit view and music before 开始探索 while a percentage progress bar shows loading; scene point lights render through a fixed light-slot pool so moving and turning no longer compile new GPU programs mid-play; the map header link now opens the GitHub repository in a new tab instead of returning to the handbook.",
    "v23: third chapter 回声剧场 opens as Loopie · 吃出一片海, a single-player eat-and-grow Canvas 2D game with a fixed power table, a 300-power success dialog and its own original looping music; it runs in a third host layer so the map and the first two chapters keep their state, the map marks three chapters playable with a third-chapter guide, and its sixteen bitmaps load as hash-named static assets (the official Loopie image is reused unchanged)."
  ],
